* BASIC and the menu share CATREADDIR and display routines. BASIC saves
* its screen/scratch before drawing and restores them before returning.
* TI BASIC read-only CALL CAT("UBE1") / CALL CAT("ROM1").
* Follows the manager in the same GROM. Device is a quoted four-character literal.
* XML >1B reads tokens; CALL return uses >0012, never the menu's EXIT.
* PARSE cannot return directly to this high GROM address: its BASIC stack
* encodes a GPL return using the address high bit. Do not use it here.
* Catalog backup reuses space not touched by the read-only directory call:
* screen 0..479 in the unused tail of the 3616-byte record buffer (>6E20),
* screen 480..767 at >7300, BASIC scratch >7420, keyboard/base >7490/>7498.
* Directory inspection does not allocate blocks or change the pending-write area.
BCLIST DATA 0,BCENTRY
       STRI 'CAT'
BCENTRY DADD 4,@>832C
       XML >1B
       CEQ >B7,@>8342
       BR BCSYNTAX
       XML >1B
       CEQ >C7,@>8342
       BR BCSYNTAX
       XML >1B
       CEQ 4,@>8342
       BR BCVALUE
       XML >1B
       ST @>8342,@>8358
       XML >1B
       ST @>8342,@>8359
       XML >1B
       ST @>8342,@>835A
       XML >1B
       ST @>8342,@>835B
       XML >1B
       CEQ >B6,@>8342
       BR BCSYNTAX
       XML >1B
       CZ @>8342
       BR BCSYNTAX
       CLR @>835D
       DCEQ >5542,@>8358
       BR BCROMNAME
       DCEQ >4531,@>835A
       BR BCVALUE
       B BCPROFILE
BCROMNAME DCEQ >524F,@>8358
       BR BCVALUE
       DCEQ >4D31,@>835A
       BR BCVALUE
       ST 1,@>835D
BCPROFILE MOVE 2,G@>A000,@>8350
       DCEQ >05FA,@>8350
       BR BCVALUE
       MOVE 1,G@>A0E5,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BR BCVALUE
       MOVE 1,G@>A0ED,@>835F
       CEQ >FF,@>835F
       BR BCVALUE
       DST @>83FA,@>835E
       DST >9838,@>83FA
       MOVE 2,@>835E,G@>7498
       MOVE 112,@>8300,G@>7420
       MOVE 8,@>8374,G@>7490
       MOVE 480,V@0,G@>6E20
       MOVE 288,V@480,G@>7300
       ST @>835D,@>8323
       ST 3,@>8374
       ST 96,@>833D
       DCLR @>832E
BCDRAW CLR @>8338
       ALL 128
       CZ @>8323
       BR BCROM
       DST >80,@>8332
       CALL CATREADDIR
       CZ @>835F
       BR BCNOTREADY
       DST >A0,@>8332
       DST 129,@>8320
       CALL CATTABLE
* Clear the PAB/summary and final metadata row from the saved screen only.
* Row 21 is still blank and lies beyond the 544-byte directory at >0080.
       MOVE 96,V@672,V@0
       MOVE 32,V@672,V@96
       MOVE 128,V@0,V@640
       B BCLABELS
* Shared metadata request: summary destination >8332, status >835F.
CATREADDIR MOVE 16,G@CATZERO,V@>40
       ST 11,V@>40
       DST @>8332,V@>42
       ST 5,V@>49
       MOVE 5,G@CATPREFIX,V@>4A
       DST >49,@>8356
       CALL >0010
       BYTE >08
       BS CATIOFAIL
       ST V@>41,@>835F
       AND >E0,@>835F
       RTN
* Shared renderer: entry >8332, first screen row >8320, font bias >833D.
CATTABLE CLR @>8322
BCUBELOOP DST @>8332,@>8350
       DST V@12(@>50),@>8324
       ST V@10(@>50),@>8337
       ST V@21(@>50),@>8339
       MOVE 10,V*>8350,@>834A
       MOVE 32,V@672,V@>FFFF(@>20)
       CZ @>834A
       BS BCEMPTY
       DST @>8320,@>8354
       ST 10,@>835E
       CALL BCNAME
       CALL BCSIZE
       CALL BCATTR
       CZ @>833D
       BR BCUBENEXT
       ST @>8337,@>835F
       AND 8,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BS CATROWMARK
       ST >21,V@30(@>20)
CATROWMARK DCLR @>8354
       ST @>8322,@>8355
       ST V@>1300(@>54),@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BS BCUBENEXT
       ST @>835F,V@29(@>20)
       B BCUBENEXT
BCEMPTY DST BCEMPTYSTR,@>8350
       DST @>8320,@>8354
       ST 7,@>835E
       CALL BCSTRING
BCUBENEXT DADD 32,@>8332
       DADD 32,@>8320
       INC @>8322
       CEQ 16,@>8322
       BR BCUBELOOP
       RTN
BCROM DCLR @>6000
       DCEQ >4346,@>6010
       BR BCNOTREADY
       DCEQ >3031,@>6012
       BR BCNOTREADY
       DST @>6014,@>8330
       DCZ @>8330
       BS BCLABELS
       DCH 510,@>8330
       BS BCNOTREADY
       DST @>832E,@>8332
       DST 129,@>8320
       CLR @>8322
BCROMLOOP DCEQ @>8330,@>8332
       BS BCLABELS
       DST @>8332,@>8350
       DSLL 4,@>8350
       DADD >6020,@>8350
       DST @>000A(@>50),@>8324
       MOVE 10,@>0000(@>50),@>834A
       DST @>8320,@>8354
       ST 10,@>835E
       CALL BCNAME
       CALL BCSIZE
       ST 1,@>8337
       CALL BCATTR
       DINC @>8332
       DADD 32,@>8320
       INC @>8322
       CEQ 16,@>8322
       BR BCROMLOOP
BCLABELS DST BCTITLE,@>8350
       DST 33,@>8354
       ST 9,@>835E
       CALL BCSTRING
       DST BCUBE,@>8350
       CZ @>8323
       BS BCDEV
       DST BCROMSTR,@>8350
BCDEV  DST 42,@>8354
       ST 4,@>835E
       CALL BCSTRING
       DST BCHEAD,@>8350
       DST 97,@>8354
       ST 29,@>835E
       CALL BCSTRING
       DST BCEXIT,@>8350
       DST 744,@>8354
       ST 12,@>835E
       CZ @>8338
       BR BCPROMPT
       CZ @>8323
       BS BCPROMPT
       DST BCPAGES,@>8350
       DST 737,@>8354
       ST 28,@>835E
BCPROMPT CALL BCSTRING
       B BCRELEASE
BCNOTREADY ALL 128
       DST BCERROR,@>8350
       DST 129,@>8354
       ST BCEND-BCERROR,@>835E
       CALL BCSTRING
       ST 1,@>8338
       B BCLABELS
BCRELEASE SCAN
       CEQ >FF,@>8375
       BR BCRELEASE
BCWAIT SCAN
       BR BCWAIT
       CEQ 13,@>8375
       BS BCRETURN
       CZ @>8338
       BR BCWAIT
       CZ @>8323
       BS BCWAIT
       CEQ >4E,@>8375
       BS BCNEXTPAGE
       CEQ >50,@>8375
       BR BCWAIT
       DCZ @>832E
       BS BCWAIT
       DSUB 16,@>832E
       B BCDRAW
BCNEXTPAGE DST @>832E,@>8350
       DADD 16,@>8350
       DCH @>8350,@>8330
       BR BCWAIT
       DST @>8350,@>832E
       B BCDRAW
BCRETURN MOVE 480,G@>6E20,V@0
       MOVE 288,G@>7300,V@480
       MOVE 112,G@>7420,@>8300
       MOVE 8,G@>7490,@>8374
       MOVE 2,G@>7498,@>83FA
       CALL >0012
* Names/numbers supplied as ASCII in >834A, length >835E, screen >8354.
BCNAME DCLR @>8356
BCNAMELP ST @>834A(@>56),@>835F
       CH 31,@>835F
       BR BCQUESTION
       CH 95,@>835F
       BR BCCHAR
BCQUESTION ST >3F,@>835F
BCCHAR ADD @>833D,@>835F
       ST @>835F,V*>8354
       DINC @>8354
       DINC @>8356
       DEC @>835E
       CZ @>835E
       BR BCNAMELP
       RTN
BCSIZE ST >30,@>8336
BCTENK DCH 9999,@>8324
       BR BCSMALL
       DSUB 10000,@>8324
       INC @>8336
       B BCTENK
BCSMALL CALL CATWORD
       ST @>8336,@>834A
       MOVE 4,@>8325,@>834B
       DST @>8320,@>8354
       DADD 24,@>8354
       ST 5,@>835E
       CALL BCNAME
       RTN
* TI attributes come from UBF1 metadata. CF01 ROM1 entries are PROGRAM.
BCATTR DST @>8320,@>8354
       DADD 11,@>8354
       DST BCPROG,@>8350
       ST 7,@>835E
       ST @>8337,@>835F
       AND 1,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BR BCSTRING
       DST BCDF,@>8350
       ST @>8337,@>835F
       AND 2,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BS BCATVAR
       DST BCIF,@>8350
BCATVAR ST @>8337,@>835F
       AND >80,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BS BCATPRINT
       DADD BCDV-BCDF,@>8350
BCATPRINT CALL BCSTRING
       DINC @>8354
       ST @>8339,@>8324
       CALL CATDEC
       MOVE 3,@>8325,@>834A
       ST 3,@>835E
* Suppress leading zeroes in record lengths, keeping the last digit.
       CEQ >30,@>834A
       BR BCATDIGITS
       ST 32,@>834A
       CEQ >30,@>834B
       BR BCATDIGITS
       ST 32,@>834B
BCATDIGITS B BCNAME
BCSTRING MOVE 1,G@>0000(@>50),@>835F
       ADD @>833D,@>835F
       ST @>835F,V*>8354
       DINC @>8350
       DINC @>8354
       DEC @>835E
       CZ @>835E
       BR BCSTRING
       RTN
BCSYNTAX CALL >001C
       BYTE >20,>2C
BCVALUE CALL >001C
       BYTE >20,>64
BCTITLE TEXT 'DEVICE:  '
BCUBE TEXT 'UBE1'
BCROMSTR TEXT 'ROM1'
BCHEAD TEXT 'FILE       TYPE         BYTES'
BCPROG TEXT 'PROGRAM'
BCDF TEXT 'DIS/FIX'
BCDV TEXT 'DIS/VAR'
BCIF TEXT 'INT/FIX'
       TEXT 'INT/VAR'
BCEMPTYSTR TEXT '(EMPTY)'
BCEXIT TEXT 'ENTER:RETURN'
BCPAGES TEXT 'P:PREV  N:NEXT  ENTER:RETURN '
BCERROR TEXT 'DEVICE CATALOG NOT READY'
BCEND
